    fix(node-create): validate --agent exists before reporting reuse (CF-051)
    
    `--agent` was reported as a successful reuse without any check, so a
    nonexistent id produced a false PASS row and work proceeded into an agent
    that does not exist. Reproduced by the foreman with a fixture `bunker` on PATH
    whose `info` always fails (PROBE_RC=1):
    
      node-create — project=demo harness=hermes server=fixture-server
        PASS  spawn — reusing ghost-agent        <-- FALSE PASS: no such agent exists
        ..    staging scripts
        FAIL  staged — cannot create node-scripts directory
      NODE INCOMPLETE (1)
    
    The operator learned the truth from an unrelated downstream failure. The same
    fixture re-run against the pre-fix revision (943ef98) prints the false reuse
    row, makes nine staging calls and exits 0 with `NODE CREATED: ghost-agent`, so
    the red is the defect and not the fixture.
    
    scripts/node-create.sh
      Step 1 now proves a supplied agent with `bunker info "$AGENT" --server
      "$SERVER"` before printing any success row and before any staging. A failure
      prints one named row and exits 1 with no `cp`/`exec` at all:
    
        FAIL  agent — <id> not found on <server> — spawn it (drop --agent) or pass
        an existing agent id
    
      `PASS  spawn — reusing …` prints only once the check passed. The no-flag path
      (spawn, then reuse) and the SPAWNED/incomplete cleanup semantics are
      unchanged: a supplied agent is never spawned, so it is never named in a
      destroy suggestion. The header comment and the usage line state the
      reuse-without-spawn contract.
    
    README.md
      One line in the node-creation section stating that `--agent ID` reuses an
      agent that must already exist, is proved with `bunker info` before any
      success row or staging, and is never spawned.
    
    tests/selftest.sh
      New §53 with three arms over one PATH stub (no network, no real bunker):
      (1) red — the id does not exist: exit 1, exactly one named `FAIL agent` row
      naming the id and the remedy, no reuse row, `info` probed, and zero
      `spawn|cp|exec` invocations in the stub's log; (2) green control — the id
      exists: the reuse row prints, staging is reached and the node is created, so
      the check is not a blanket refusal of `--agent`; (3) pre-fix control — the
      943ef98 revision re-run against the same fixture still prints the false
      `PASS  spawn — reusing ghost-agent` and stages anyway, so the arm keeps a
      demonstrable red. Rows are asserted by name, never by the bare substring
      FAIL. The two existing bunker stubs that node-create reaches with `--agent`
      (CF-075 §16, CF-159 §36) now answer `info` so they still exercise what they
      name.
    
    Two files outside the brief's fence were required to make the mandated gate
    green, both disclosed here:
    
    docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md
      §53's mapping row plus the arm census (55 -> 56 arms, 52 -> 53 numbered
      sections). `tests/selftest.sh` §39 grades this table against the tree, so a
      new section cannot land without it; `bash docs/audits/cf198-section-mapping.sh`
      now prints `RESULT: OK` with `arms_plan=56 arms_tree=56`.
    
    scripts/panel_loop.py
      Pre-existing red at this HEAD, unrelated to CF-051: ruff 0.15.22 reports
      `F841 Local variable 'rc' is assigned to but never used` at :114 (the file
      landed that way in f0ca317, and the finding is present in the HEAD blob), and
      §51 grades the tracked python surface, so the suite could not reach PASS on
      this host before the change. Dropped the unused assignment to the
      never-read `subprocess.call` status; behavior is identical and
      `ruff check $(git ls-files '*.py')` now reports `All checks passed!`.
    
    Gate, run after the last edit in this checkout:
    
      bash tests/selftest.sh
      ...
      53. node-create refuses a --agent that does not exist, before any staging (CF-051)
        PASS  missing --agent -> named FAIL agent, exit 1, info probed, zero staging calls
        PASS  existing --agent -> reuse row printed, staging reached, node created (exit 0)
        PASS  pre-fix revision reports the false reuse row and stages anyway (fixture detects CF-051)
    
      SELFTEST: PASS
    
    380 PASS rows, 0 counted failures, exit 0. `bash -n` clean on both shell files
    touched. No GitReins task was created or completed, nothing was pushed.
